": ["No expert rater lists this race; treated as safe for the party holding the seat.", "Incumbent Ben Cline (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Republican incumbent Ben Cline seeks another term in a Shenandoah Valley–anchored district that leans Republican by about twelve points. He faces Democrat Beth Macy, a former journalist whose campaign has drawn attention for its fundraising and for national Democrats' claims that the seat is newly competitive.\n\nThe evidence still favors Cline decisively. The district's lean, his incumbency, and a late-September live-caller poll showing him far ahead all point the same way, and prediction markets price his win at roughly 93 percent. Macy has raised more money than the incumbent, which keeps the race from being a total formality, but a fundraising edge alone rarely overcomes a double-digit structural deficit. A Cline victory remains the clear expectation.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0375, "margin": -14.4}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0454, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0463, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0654, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0527, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0505, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0614, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0306, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0328, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0472, "margin": -13.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0358, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.036, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0359, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0299, "margin": -14.0}]}